# A font is bytes, not text.
#
# The same rule and the same reason as `test/fixtures/save/.gitattributes`:
# this repository is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, and a TTF
# contains 0x0D and 0x0A bytes throughout its tables. Left to line-ending
# normalization the file is silently corrupted on checkout, the font fails to
# parse, and `loadRealFont()` reports the harness fault it exists to report —
# on Linux only, from a repository that looks correct on the machine that
# committed it.
#
# Git's binary auto-detection currently gets this right; the committed blobs
# were verified byte-identical to the SDK originals. This makes it a rule
# rather than a coincidence.
*.ttf binary

# The licence is text and should normalize like any other text file.
*.txt text
